<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">6 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 6 May, from 1527 to 1994.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/rome" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rome.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1527">1527 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">499 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Imperial troops sack Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Unpaid troops of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> stormed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, killing thousands and looting churches while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-clement-vii">Pope Clement VII</a> sheltered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/castel-santangelo">Castel Sant'Angelo</a>. The sack scattered Rome's artists and humbled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1840">1840 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">186 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Penny Black becomes valid for postage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s prepaid adhesive stamps could now be used on letters. Paying a flat penny in advance, rather than charging recipients by distance, made post cheap and predictable.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1882">1882 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">144 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Chester Arthur signs the Chinese Exclusion Act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The law suspended the immigration of Chinese labourers and barred Chinese immigrants from citizenship. It was the first major US law to exclude a group by nationality and was repealed only in 1943.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1889">1889 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">137 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Paris Exposition Universelle opens beneath the Eiffel Tower</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The world's fair marking the centenary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a> opened in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>. Its entrance arch, Gustave Eiffel's iron tower, was then the tallest structure in the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1910">1910 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">116 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward VII dies and George V becomes king</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Edward VII died at Buckingham Palace after a nine-year reign. Known for his diplomacy and support for the Entente Cordiale, he gave his name to the Edwardian era.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1937">1937 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">89 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hindenburg airship bursts into flames at Lakehurst</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The German airship Hindenburg caught fire while mooring in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a>, killing 36 people. Newsreel film and radio coverage of the disaster ended public faith in passenger airships.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1954">1954 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">72 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Roger Bannister runs the first sub-four-minute mile</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On a windy evening at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a>'s Iffley Road track, the medical student Roger Bannister ran the mile in 3 minutes 59.4 seconds, helped by pacemakers Chris Brasher and Chris Chataway.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1994">1994 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">32 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Channel Tunnel is formally opened</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-ii">Elizabeth II</a> and President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francois-mitterrand">François Mitterrand</a> opened the 50 km rail tunnel under the Channel. It gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> its first fixed link to the Continent since the Ice Age.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 6 May <span class="n">11</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-holy-roman-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-ii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry II, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="tp">973–1024</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-x"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-innocent-x.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Innocent X</span><span class="tp">1574–1655</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-duke-of-mantua"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-i-duke-of-mantua.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles I, Duke of Mantua</span><span class="tp">1580–1637</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/andre-massena"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/andre-massena.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">André Masséna</span><span class="tp">1758–1817</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/maximilien-robespierre"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maximilien-robespierre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Maximilien Robespierre</span><span class="tp">1758–1794</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-grand-duke-of-tuscany"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-iii-grand-duke-of-tuscany.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ferdinand III, Grand Duke of Tuscany</span><span class="tp">1769–1824</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/djemal-pasha"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/djemal-pasha.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Djemal Pasha</span><span class="tp">1872–1922</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/konrad-henlein"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/konrad-henlein.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Konrad Henlein</span><span class="tp">1898–1945</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/zayed-bin-sultan-al-nahyan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/zayed-bin-sultan-al-nahyan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Zayed bin Sultan Al Nahyan</span><span class="tp">1918–2004</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/samuel-doe"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/samuel-doe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Samuel Doe</span><span class="tp">1951–1990</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tony-blair"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tony-blair.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tony Blair</span><span class="tp">b. 1953</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 6 May <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/qian-liu"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/qian-liu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Qian Liu</span><span class="tp">852–932</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/dieric-bouts"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dieric-bouts.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Dieric Bouts</span><span class="tp">c. 1415–1475</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-iii-duke-of-bourbon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-iii-duke-of-bourbon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles III, Duke of Bourbon</span><span class="tp">1490–1527</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francois-de-laval"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francois-de-laval.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">François de Laval</span><span class="tp">1623–1708</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-paula-santander"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francisco-de-paula-santander.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francisco de Paula Santander</span><span class="tp">1792–1840</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alexander-von-humboldt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alexander-von-humboldt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alexander von Humboldt</span><span class="tp">1769–1859</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/maria-montessori"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maria-montessori.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Maria Montessori</span><span class="tp">1870–1952</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jozsef-mindszenty"><img src="/images/encycl